** |\n| \\(B\\!-\\!C\\) | \\(-1\\) | No |\n| \\(B\\!-\\!D\\) | \\(\\infty\\) | No |\n| \\(B\\!-\\!E\\) | \\(-\\tfrac12\\) | **Yes** |\n| \\(B\\!-\\!F\\) | \\(0\\) | No |\n| \\(C\\!-\\!D\\) | \\(-2\\) | **Yes** |\n| \\(C\\!-\\!E\\) | \\(0\\) | No |\n| \\(C\\!-\\!F\\) | \\(\\infty\\) | No |\n| \\(D\\!-\\!E\\) | \\(-1\\) | No |\n| \\(D\\!-\\!F\\) | \\(-1\\) | No |\n| \\(E\\!-\\!F\\) | \\(-1\\) | No |\n\nHence the only sunny lines that contain **at least two** of the six points are  \n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\ell_{AF}&:\\; y=x \\qquad\\text{(through }A,F\\text{)},\\\\[2pt]\n\\ell_{BE}&:\\; y=-\\tfrac12 x+\\tfrac52 \\qquad\\text{(through }B,E\\text{)},\\\\[2pt]\n\\ell_{CD}&:\\; y=-2x+3 \\qquad\\text{(through }C,D\\text{)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 2.  Choice of the non\u2011sunny line  \n\nA non\u2011sunny line must be horizontal (\\(y=\\text{const}\\)), vertical (\\(x=\\text{const}\\)), or have slope \\(-1\\) (parallel to \\(x+y=0\\)).  \nThe horizontal line  \n\n\\[\n\\ell_{h}:\\; y=1\n\\]\n\ncontains the three points \\(A(1,1),\\;C(2,1),\\;E(3,1)\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 3.  Completing the covering with two sunny lines  \n\nThe remaining points are \\(B(1,2),\\;D(1,3),\\;F(2,2)\\).\n\n* The line \\(\\ell_{AF}: y=x\\) (sunny) passes through \\(A\\) and \\(F\\); it therefore covers \\(F\\) (the point \\(A\\) is already covered by \\(\\ell_{h}\\), which is allowed).\n* The line \\(\\ell_{BD}: y=-2x+5\\) (sunny) passes through \\(B\\) and \\(D\\); it covers both \\(B\\) and \\(D\\).\n\nBoth \\(\\ell_{AF}\\) and \\(\\ell_{BD}\\) have slopes \\(1\\) and \\(-2\\) respectively, which are different from \\(0,\\infty,-1\\); consequently they are sunny.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 4.  Verification  \n\nThe three distinct lines are  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{aligned}\nL_{1}&:\\; y = x \\quad\\text{(sunny