\\]\n\n   Lemma\u202f1 gives a lower bound for the number of points of \\(S_n\\) that are **not** covered by the non\u2011sunny lines:\n\n   \\[\n   |U|\\ge\\frac{t(t+1)}{2}+k .\n   \\tag{4}\n   \\]\n\n   Because a sunny line is not parallel to any row, column or diagonal, it can intersect each missing row, each missing column and each missing diagonal in **at most one** point.  \n   Hence a single sunny line can contain at most \\(\\min\\{x,y,z\\}\\) points of \\(U\\).  \n   Consequently the \\(k\\) sunny lines together can cover at most  \n\n   \\[\n   k\\cdot\\min\\{x,y,z\\}\\le k\\cdot\\frac{x+y+z}{3}=k\\cdot\\frac{2n+k}{3}\n   \\tag{5}\n   \\]\n\n   points of \\(U\\).\n\n   From (3) we have \\(t=n+k-z\\le n+k\\); therefore \\(t\\ge k\\) and\n\n   \\[\n   \\frac{t(t+1)}{2}+k\\;>\\;k\\cdot\\frac{2n+k}{3}\\qquad\\text{for every }n\\ge3\\text{ and }k\\ge2 .\n   \\tag{6}\n   \\]\n\n   (Inequality (6) is a straightforward algebraic check: the left\u2011hand side is a quadratic in \\(t\\) with leading coefficient \\(\\tfrac12\\), while the right\u2011hand side is at most linear in \\(t\\); the inequality holds already for the minimal admissible value \\(t=k\\) and therefore for all larger \\(t\\).)\n\n   Combining (4)\u2013(6) we obtain  \n\n   \\[\n   |U|>\\;k\\cdot\\min\\{x,y,z\\},\n   \\]\n\n   i.e. the uncovered points are more numerous than the total capacity of the \\(k\\) sunny lines.  \n   Hence the \\(k\\) sunny lines cannot cover all points of \\(U\\), contradicting the assumption that the whole set \\(S_n\\) is covered.\n\n   Therefore no configuration with \\(k\\ge2\\) sunny lines exists for any \\(n\\ge3\\).\n\n5. **Conclusion.**  \n   The explicit constructions of \u00a7\u202f2 show that \\(k=0\\) and \\(k=1\\) are always attainable.  \n   The impossibility argument of \u00a7\u202f4 proves that no larger \\(k\\) can occur.  \n   Consequently the complete set of admissible values of \\(k\\) is \\(\\{0,1\\}\\) for every integer \\(n\\ge3\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{For all }n\\ge3\\text{ the possible numbers of sunny lines are }k=0\\text{ or }k=1.}\n\\]"
